            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "sensorhandler.cpp",
                    "line": 1631,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nagavarapu Sai Pavan",
                        "email": "saipavann@ami.com",
                        "username": "saipavann27"
                    },
                    "message": "Alarm states are dynamic \u2014 they change whenever a reading crosses a threshold. This means the first response is correct, but all subsequent responses for the same sensor return stale data.\n\nEX:\n\n1. Sensor 0x10 reads 28\u00b0C, upper warning threshold is 45\u00b0C \u2192 alarm is `false`. Cached.\n2. Threshold is later changed to 20\u00b0C \u2192 28\u00b0C now exceeds it \u2192 alarm should be `true`.\n3. Next call returns cached `false` \u2014 incorrect.\n\nBetter If may fetch fresh data"
                }
            ],
